A||N||12||MickeyAsh||Question for my fellow audiophiles||||3||
Z||000000||MickeyAsh||07-10-2001||10:01 PM||||So, I'm in the process of cutting my firewall for my two subs behind my seats, when i see daylight. And I'm like "**** !" so I stopped, and surveyed the size of the holes, and determined they could be filled. So for those of you out there who have also done this project, which did you go with, MDF or Fiberglass to make the area airtight?||||reg||3
Z||000001||sombre||07-10-2001||11:23 PM||||  I used fiberglass but they are untested as of yet...I'm just getting the interior back together and still have to mount amps,eq,radio....hope it holds.<P>                           Greg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||07-10-2001||11:32 PM||||Though I have never done this, I assume, since people are making sub boxes completely out of fiberglass, that if you do that it should be just fine.  You just want to make sure that you prep the area that the fiberglass is going to have to stick to very well.  Scuff the paint up really good and make sure that it is very clean of dirt and grease/oils.  Wipe some lacquer thinner or xylol on it and then wipe it off with a clean rag.  This will loosen any crap that's there and it will be wiped clean.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MickeyAsh||07-10-2001||11:40 PM||||Another thought just crossed my mind... has anyone tried Bondo? I was  discussing it with my friend, and you could easily use duct tape or screen to cover any holes and then bondo over that... hmm...||||reg||1
Z||000004||MickeyAsh||07-10-2001||11:41 PM||||Also where can I get fiberglass, in case I decide to go in that direction? lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||07-11-2001||12:42 AM||||Wal-Mart baby, why go anywhere else? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>WM's auto department has a kit that will do you fine for about $15, made by Bondo. Get an oil change while you're there. Tell em stimpy sent you...||||reg||1
Z||000006||MickeyAsh||07-11-2001||12:48 AM||||Kickass, so what, I just mix it up, slap it on, and let it dry?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||07-11-2001||02:34 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MickeyAsh:<BR><B>Kickass, so what, I just mix it up, slap it on, and let it dry?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes...use enough hardener.<BR>I'll give away some some tips here...don't bother with fiberglass mat.  layer after layer the stuff is time consuming.<BR>Call up JC Whitney or visit an audio place and order trunk liner carpet.  Use this instead of the mat.  It is thick and gets rock hard. One layer will do it!  Coat the metal and one side of the carpet...stick it on and let dry.  Then coat the crap out of the other side...use plenty of resin...it will absorb it.  Home Cheapo has fiberglass kits and gallons of resin too, otherwise a NAPA store will have the stuff.<P>Cutting the firewall...there is probably a reason it is double walled there.  Dunno.  I'm short so I stuck 2 10s and 4 8s in my car and left the firewall alone(but stripped the carpet off of course.  I still have some room behind my seats.<P>Oh, to finish off the rough carpet(the downside of the carpet) buy BondoGlass or Napa's short hair fiberglass filler.  Use like bondo, but very strong--you can use this with a screen mesh too.<P><BR>Joe<BR>3000+ watts RMS<BR>3400 series 300hp<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||MickeyAsh||07-12-2001||12:22 AM||||Ehh... unfortunately I don't have time to put out an order for anything, i'm doing this on vacation... so I finished ripping out the firewalls today, and started with the mats and resin... im on the 4th mat layer, i want it nice and thick... ill put on two more layers tomorrow and let it dry while I work out the frameworks... if anyone has any advice, yell at me. While I'm here, I'll give you all a laugh... I, being the unexperienced person I am, put the polyester resin/hardener mixture in a plastic solo cup... and im sure many of you have already guessed, it ate it's way through in a few minutes... fortunately it was only over my left thigh, and only got on my shorts... I'd hate to have that stuff on anything... valuable... if you catch my drift... ::shudders::||||reg||1
