Z||000012||gtcash||07-13-2001||12:47 AM||||Did anyone tell you to use those cheap throw away rubber gloves? How about a gallon of acetone for cleanup?<BR>In the late 50's I read about resin being used to fix rust on cars...in Calif...I ordered the stuff, I was the FIRST in my neighbor hood in Chicago...I dipped the glass into a quart container of resin with my bare hands, kinda squeezed it out with my fingers and wiped it onto the rusted area...I heard a crakling noise and looked down and that quart container I had between my legs was smoking! I touched it, and boy was it HOT! Now, realizing I had this crap all over my hands, I ran to the sink and tried to wash it off with water...Try that...NOT!<BR>Hey, good luck with your project.||||reg||1
